From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AESL Android CI <ci@active-esl.invalid>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 13:10:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] soong: Allow CI to bound builder Go heap

Large Android product graphs can otherwise consume all available host memory
while soong_build analyzes Android.bp files. Pass a separately named build
setting into the sanitized builder environment as the standard Go runtime
GOMEMLIMIT variable.

The limit remains opt-in, so normal Android builds are unchanged.
---
 ui/build/soong.go | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ui/build/soong.go b/ui/build/soong.go
index a271246..eb60c32 100644
--- a/ui/build/soong.go
+++ b/ui/build/soong.go
@@ -241,5 +241,8 @@ func (pb primaryBuilder) invocation() bootstrap.PrimaryBuilderInvocation {
 		// https://github.com/golang/proposal/blob/master/design/24543-non-cooperative-preemption.md
 		invocationEnv["GODEBUG"] = "asyncpreemptoff=1"
+	}
+	if memoryLimit := os.Getenv("SOONG_GOMEMLIMIT"); memoryLimit != "" {
+		invocationEnv["GOMEMLIMIT"] = memoryLimit
 	}
 
 	var allArgs []string
-- 
2.39.5
